#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The program below can be used to demonstrate the operation of B<strcmp>()  "
"(when given two arguments) and B<strncmp>()  (when given three arguments).  "
"First, some examples using B<strcmp>():"
msgstr ""
"Das nachfolgende Programm kann zur Darstellung der Aktion von B<strcmp>() "
"(wenn zwei Argumente übergeben werden) und B<strncmp>() (wenn drei Argumente "
"übergeben werden) verwandt werden. Zuerst ein paar Beispiele zum Einsatz von "
"B<strcmp>():"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ B<./string_comp ABC ABC>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> and E<lt>str2E<gt> are equal\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABC AB>      # \\[aq]C\\[aq] is ASCII 67; \\[aq]C\\[aq] - \\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq] = 67\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> is greater than E<lt>str2E<gt> (67)\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABA ABZ>     # \\[aq]A\\[aq] is ASCII 65; \\[aq]Z\\[aq] is ASCII 90\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> is less than E<lt>str2E<gt> (-25)\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABJ ABC>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> is greater than E<lt>str2E<gt> (7)\n"
"$ .B</string_comp $\\[aq]\\[rs]201\\[aq] A>   # 0201 - 0101 = 0100 (or 64 decimal)\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> is greater than E<lt>str2E<gt> (64)\n"
msgstr ""
"$ B<./string_comp ABC ABC>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> und E<lt>str2E<gt> sind identisch\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABC AB>      # »C« ist ASCII 67; »C« - »\\[rs]0« = 67\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> ist größer als E<lt>str2E<gt> (67)\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABA ABZ>     # »A« ist ASCII 65; »Z« ist ASCII 90\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> ist kleiner als E<lt>str2E<gt> (-25)\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABJ ABC>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> ist größer als E<lt>str2E<gt> (7)\n"
"$ .B</string_comp $\\[aq]\\[rs]201\\[aq] A>   # 0201 - 0101 = 0100 (oder 64 dezimal)\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> ist größer als E<lt>str2E<gt> (64)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The last example uses B<bash>(1)-specific syntax to produce a string "
"containing an 8-bit ASCII code; the result demonstrates that the string "
"comparison uses unsigned characters."
msgstr ""
"Das letzte Beispiel verwendet eine B<bash>(1)-spezifische Syntax, um eine "
"Zeichenkette zu erzeugen, die einen 8-Bit-ASCII-Code enthält; das Ergebnis "
"zeigt, dass der Zeichenkettenvergleich vorzeichenlose Zeichen verwendet."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "And then some examples using B<strncmp>():"
msgstr "Und dann ein paar Beispiele mit B<strncmp>():"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ B<./string_comp ABC AB 3>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> is greater than E<lt>str2E<gt> (67)\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABC AB 2>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> and E<lt>str2E<gt> are equal in the first 2 bytes\n"
msgstr ""
"$ B<./string_comp ABC AB 3>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> ist größer als E<lt>str2E<gt> (67)\n"
"$ B<./string_comp ABC AB 2>\n"
"E<lt>str1E<gt> und E<lt>str2E<gt> sind identisch in den ersten 2 Byte\n"

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "Program source"
msgstr "Programmquelltext"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"/* string_comp.c\n"
"\\&\n"
"   Licensed under GNU General Public License v2 or later.\n"
"*/\n"
"#include E<lt>stdio.hE<gt>\n"
"#include E<lt>stdlib.hE<gt>\n"
"#include E<lt>string.hE<gt>\n"
"\\&\n"
"int\n"
"main(int argc, char *argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"    int res;\n"
"\\&\n"
"    if (argc E<lt> 3) {\n"
"        fprintf(stderr, \"Usage: %s E<lt>str1E<gt> E<lt>str2E<gt> [E<lt>lenE<gt>]\\[rs]n\", argv[0]);\n"
"        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"    }\n"
"\\&\n"
"    if (argc == 3)\n"
"        res = strcmp(argv[1], argv[2]);\n"
"    else\n"
"        res = strncmp(argv[1], argv[2], atoi(argv[3]));\n"
"\\&\n"
"    if (res == 0) {\n"
"        printf(\"E<lt>str1E<gt> and E<lt>str2E<gt> are equal\");\n"
"        if (argc E<gt> 3)\n"
"            printf(\" in the first %d bytes\\[rs]n\", atoi(argv[3]));\n"
"        printf(\"\\[rs]n\");\n"
"    } else if (res E<lt> 0) {\n"
"        printf(\"E<lt>str1E<gt> is less than E<lt>str2E<gt> (%d)\\[rs]n\", res);\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        printf(\"E<lt>str1E<gt> is greater than E<lt>str2E<gt> (%d)\\[rs]n\", res);\n"
"    }\n"
"\\&\n"
"    exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"/* string_comp.c\n"
"\\&\n"
"   Lizensiert unter der GNU General Public License v2 oder neuer.\n"
"*/\n"
"#include E<lt>stdio.hE<gt>\n"
"#include E<lt>stdlib.hE<gt>\n"
"#include E<lt>string.hE<gt>\n"
"\\&\n"
"int\n"
"main(int argc, char *argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"    int res;\n"
"\\&\n"
"    if (argc E<lt> 3) {\n"
"        fprintf(stderr, \"Aufruf: %s E<lt>zeichenkette1E<gt> E<lt>zeichenkette2E<gt> [E<lt>länE<gt>]\\[rs]n\", argv[0]);\n"
"        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"    }\n"
"\\&\n"
"    if (argc == 3)\n"
"        res = strcmp(argv[1], argv[2]);\n"
"    else\n"
"        res = strncmp(argv[1], argv[2], atoi(argv[3]));\n"
"\\&\n"
"    if (res == 0) {\n"
"        printf(\"E<lt>zeichenkette1E<gt> und E<lt>zeichenkette2E<gt> sind gleich\");\n"
"        if (argc E<gt> 3)\n"
"            printf(\" in den ersten %d byte\\[rs]n\", atoi(argv[3]));\n"
"        printf(\"\\[rs]n\");\n"
"    } else if (res E<lt> 0) {\n"
"        printf(\"E<lt>zeichenkette1E<gt> ist kleiner als E<lt>zeichenkette2E<gt> (%d)\\[rs]n\", res);\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        printf(\"E<lt>zeichenkette1E<gt> ist größer als E<lt>zeichenkette2E<gt> (%d)\\[rs]n\", res);\n"
"    }\n"
"\\&\n"
"    exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n"
"}\n"

